; Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen","body":[{"what":"halfLife","says":"3.6 hours (range 2.6–5.3 hours)"},{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Oxidative deamination, N-acetylation, O-demethylation, conjugation, other pathways"},{"what":"turnsInto","says":"TMPA; TMPAA; TMPE; Others"}],"figures":"Mescaline"},"uses":{"text":"Mescaline is used recreationally, spiritually, and medically. It is typically taken orally.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Mescaline","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mescaline#Use_and_effects","routes":"Oral, smoking, insufflation, intravenous","figures":"Mescaline"},"sideEffects":{"text":"Side effects of mescaline include fatigue, weakness, impaired concentration, restlessness, tension, anxiety, panic, and social discomfort and avoidance, headache, pupil dilation, nausea, vomiting, sweating, trembling, discomfort, feeling hot or cold, palpitations, chest and neck pains, shortness of breath, increased heart rate and blood pressure, and increased body temperature, among others.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Mescaline","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mescaline#Adverse_effects"}}